{"id":"20260825T192210.336380634Z-318c4f9e","time":"2026-08-25T19:22:10.336380634Z","session_id":"session-20260825T191536.559000665Z","task_id":"task-1787685336559236552","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  The abandoned-worktree check treats a candidate directory containing only this tool's own artefacts as if it held the user's work, so a repository is reported as holding abandoned work when it holds none, and nothing offers to clean it up.\n\nA candidate whose contents are entirely artefacts this tool created must not be described as holding work, and must be removable automatically. A candidate holding anything the user could have written must still be preserved and reported for a person to decide. Dot-directories beside a candidate are this tool's own and are not candidates.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] checkAbandonedWorktrees currently treats every non-live, non-empty directory under the sibling worktree root as an abandoned candidate holding files. (internal/setup/checks.go:checkAbandonedWorktrees) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The existing repair rechecks only literal emptiness, so it cannot remove a directory containing solely a linked-worktree `.git` marker. (internal/setup/checks.go:isEmptyDir and removeAll) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Candidate creation uses `git worktree add`, and CreateWorktree treats the candidate’s `.git` entry as the marker that the workspace already exists. (internal/gitx/git.go:CreateWorktree) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The push guard created by Sensei Code is placed in a `.guard` directory beside the candidate workspace rather than inside it. (internal/workflow/engine.go:runCandidate) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The TUI `/setup` path only renders the readiness report, while the CLI `setup --apply` path explicitly invokes repairs and then re-inspects. (internal/tui/model.go:Model.senseiCommand and cmd/sensei-code/setup.go:runSetup) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The current checkout has no focused abandoned-worktree regression tests under internal/setup. (internal/setup tests) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei requires candidate disposition to be decided and its evidence to outlive removal. (candidate cleanup lifecycle) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Sensei requires preservation of every changed file for reviewer judgment, including files a worker created. (candidate contents) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] Scoped preflight examined both planned files, classified the change as low risk, and found no directly anchored governing rule; confidence remains low. (internal/setup/checks.go and internal/setup/setup_test.go) — source: graph\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: bounded-knowledge-gap\n"}
